  "title": "Betty F NDE 4938",
  "date": "11/23/2010",
  "content": "My father died on the evening of 11/21/2010. It was the first time I've ever seen anyone die, or had anyone die, and he was the closest person to my life. On the morning of 11/23/2010, I passed out/fainted. I had two fainting spells. The first one was a complete blackout, no memory or recollection when I was out. The second one has a memory. When I awoke, I had a vivid memory of what I saw and it actually felt as if I had been somewhere, and that I had returned from that 'happy place' and very loving. It did not feel like a dream at all - it felt I was there, and it was incredibly 'happy', exhilarating, and I was not content coming back to reality. The memory is vivid, stronger than a dream felt alert, aware, real, like being there, felt like I was awake, easy to recall. I saw people but no faces, just dark/shadowed bodies in the background. A person was next to me in the light - shining person, who looked like it might be a woman, don't know - but she had an enlightening feeling about her. People felt real, felt like I floated back to reality, floated through an area. I don't know what this was other than it felt like I was somewhere else physically.",
